## Induction Heating sample: torus inductor
## Required labels: source, sink (sidesets on terminal faces)
## Optional labels: workpiece, air
##
## Creates a torus by sweeping a circle along an arc (not 'create torus',
## which produces a closed surface with no terminal faces).
## The sweep angle < 360 leaves two open faces for source/sink.
##
## Usage: Solve -> Radia-NGSolve -> Induction Heating

reset

# Cross-section circle (R_minor = 0.01 m, centered at R_major = 0.11 m)
create vertex 0.10 0 0
create vertex 0.12 0 0
create vertex 0.11 0 0.01
create curve arc three vertex 1 3 2
create vertex 0.11 0 -0.01
create curve arc three vertex 2 4 1
create surface curve 1 2

# Sweep 350 degrees around Z axis (leaves 10-degree gap for terminals)
sweep surface 1 axis 0 0 0 0 0 1 angle 350

# Mesh
volume 1 scheme tetmesh
volume 1 size auto factor 5
mesh volume 1

# Material block
block 1 add volume 1
block 1 name "coil"

# Terminal faces: the two planar ends created by the incomplete sweep
# Surface 1 = start face (source), Surface 3 = end face (sink)
sideset 1 add surface 1
sideset 1 name "source"
sideset 2 add surface 3
sideset 2 name "sink"
